[start-outcomes] After this part you should be able to
1. state what EC2 treats as a column and how short and slender columns fail, and classify a column as braced or unbraced;
2. find the clear height and the relative flexibilities k_1 and k_2 at the ends of a column, and its effective length l_0 by EC2 Eq. 5.15 or 5.16;
3. calculate the slenderness ratio λ about each axis and the limit λ_{lim} , with the right n and r_m ;
4. classify a column as non-slender or slender about each axis, and find the slips in someone else’s check.
